<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Putin agrees to resume three-way talks with Kyiv and Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d66b56b6029ea8eee7e9033e036d99f14d77e7ed1999506e09c578b697636b27</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/putin-agrees-to-resume-three-way-talks-with-kyiv-and-washington" /><summary type="html">President ⁠Volodymyr Zelenskiy ​said on Wednesday ​that Ukraine supported a US proposal for ​three-way talks ‌with Russia ⁠and the United ‌States at the level ⁠of negotiators to be held as soon ​as possible, preferably ‌no later than early November. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe, Russia and Eurasia Programme at Chatham House, says that "it's not clear whether Putin would meet Trump and Zelensky", adding that "meeting Zelensky is the last thing that Putin would be prepared to do".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump faces fresh questions over ties to 'humanitarian' Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:908b8a28278ea77fb0f0b8280a7c9ca9e0efe71221feda12b98776a00a262965</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T18:53:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-faces-fresh-questions-over-ties-to-humanitarian-putin" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's pivot away from Ukraine has triggered fresh questions about his attachment to Russian leader Vladimir Putin, the man a top American envoy flattered on Wednesday as a "humanitarian. Trump has cast his dealings with Putin as part of a mega-deal that has secured the release of American detainee Stephen Hubbard -- and which Trump says will end Russia's war on Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kremlin says 'ready' to resume 3-way talks with US and Ukraine mid-November</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80e278f688c75b8e031542d3c7018e431fe393cdd76bdbee5c34e0735bdde7b6</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:51:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kremlin-says-ready-to-resume-3-way-talks-with-us-and-ukraine-mid-november" /><summary type="html">Moscow is ready to resume trilateral US-Ukraine-Russia talks next month, the Kremlin said Wednesday after President Vladimir Putin met with US envoy Steve Witkoff in Russia. FRANCE 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Prosecutors search European Parliament offices of far-right Patriots bloc in graft probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdcff48f2b1304ead802ed2833786374a543e821ff5718f9976ffc05c196321e</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:07:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-prosecutors-search-european-parliament-offices-of-far-right-patriots-bloc-in-graft-probe" /><summary type="html">EU prosecutors on Wednesday searched offices belonging to the far-right Patriots parliamentary group as part of a graft probe into the bloc’s dissolved predecessor, Identity and Democracy, which brought together several European far-right parties including French presidential candidate Marine Le Pen’s National Rally.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia both ready to resume trilateral talks with US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7eb65585e6d9f1d8fe3205c4d704671d3f6723e59a41707b22f739082b1b6b80</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:46:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-zelensky-proposes-freezing-front-with-russia-first-step-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Russia on Wednesday said they are both ready to resume trilateral talks with the United States. The news comes after US envoy Steve Witkoff separately met with Volodymyr Zelensky and Vladimir Putin on two consecutive days.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e0f5e721b5b4c1b4aa3775ec0288168fbc58e5776b67d0b9c617ec1e125190d</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:44:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.</summary></entry><entry><title>Greece: Protesters demand increased funding for public education</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77ff1808e270e32751c0e4e36a0a45a6d4448ed3c8b847727c65a9b1bc7379e6</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:25:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/greece-protesters-demand-increased-funding-for-public-education" /><summary type="html">Students, teachers and civil servants are demonstrating in Greece today, protesting over staff shortages, poor infrastructure and the cost of living. Dozens of students have set up tents in the Square facing Parliament, in Athens, and on a pedestrian street in Thessaloniki on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Athens, Nathalie Savaricas.</summary></entry><entry><title>Portugal police clear demonstrators from protest camps against cost of housing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02f8a1ea9de256082fd294514b40b020cdcc078971eb3a057864fc4f1e78529d</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T12:31:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-portugal-police-clear-demonstrators-from-protest-camps-against-cost-of-housing--71256b40ecc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-portugal-police-clear-demonstrators-from-protest-camps-against-cost-of-housing" /><summary type="html">Portuguese demonstrators have been protesting against the cost of housing in the country. They are opposed to recent measures announced by the government and are calling for a new gathering in the coming days, despite police clearing protest camps.</summary></entry><entry><title>US envoy Steve Witkoff thanks Vladimir Putin for diesel deal at Ukraine talks in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:714fb6f956e57415033fa8215a6f16858453cbd1212222a71082a03bf1543749</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T11:07:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-envoy-steve-witkoff-thanks-vladimir-putin-for-diesel-deal-at-ukraine-talks-in-russia--30521be1972e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-envoy-steve-witkoff-thanks-vladimir-putin-for-diesel-deal-at-ukraine-talks-in-russia" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff is in Saint Petersburg, holding talks with Russian president Vladimir Putin. The face to face meeting comes after he met with Ukraine's president and other European leaders in Oslo. Witkoff is due to return to the Norwegian capital after his visit to Russia. Washington seeks to breathe new life into US-led efforts to end the war. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Kethevane Gorjestani.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine talks: US envoy meets Vladimir Putin in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95f23f34041207dd1bf83a1adb5f19d8d850dfe023d77dcf26e4a6ad485a83e8</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T11:04:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-us-envoy-meets-vladimir-putin-in-russia--fcf1a297b9ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-us-envoy-meets-vladimir-putin-in-russia" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff held talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin in St. Petersburg on Wednesday about Moscow’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine, as US President Donald Trump pushes Kyiv to make a deal that stops the fighting. The day before, the American official had met with Ukraine's Volodymyr Zelensky in Oslo, Norway. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine talks: What progress after US envoy meeting with Zelensky?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aa5ccd4b3b619389db3bf9842478ac792dfa4fc4d1c4f33758631e479333585</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:58:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-what-progress-after-us-envoy-met-with-zelensky--e9f78446a0bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-what-progress-after-us-envoy-met-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">US Special Envoy Steve Witkoff is headed to Russia today to meet with Russian President Vladimir Putin for peace talks. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, on his end, met with the US official in Norway Tuesday. What progress has been made in Oslo? Ophélie Jacobson explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy deploys army and approves tougher anti-riot laws after violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c910ff9b99b153ddb3f935d009d63ac61f3163e9ca4be23af558b756ae8ce55c</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:57:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/italy-deploys-army-and-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-violence--92b0ab3689c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/italy-deploys-army-and-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-violence" /><summary type="html">Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni on Tuesday announced the deployment of 500 troops to Milan to assist police following clashes in the city. Meloni said a cabinet meeting also approved measures to make the detention of minors easier and to impose fines on their parents for any damage. Story by Morgan Ayre.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin announces release of US citizen Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c1fda9f710c4372333fc562851ae01a76da2224e0cf2b03417d5031398dba87</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T04:29:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky--f8a9a6da7c99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">US special envoy Steve Witkoff met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Saint Petersburg on Wednesday after talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky in Oslo. Putin said during the meeting that Russia had released US citizen Stephen Hubbard, who had been imprisoned for years in Russia after being charged of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: French authorities ban protests in several cities and parts of Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:774f97b4905c8bede1f08f2955992afb74b798312d2338168362c4eaa853977c</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T00:45:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-live-french-pm-lecornu-to-meet-with-unions-ahead-of-new-protests--4ab6b3d7a9b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-live-french-pm-lecornu-to-meet-with-unions-ahead-of-new-protests" /><summary type="html">Local authorities on Wednesday banned protests planned in several French cities in the next few days – from Toulon in the south to Le Havre in the north – and also imposed night-time curfews in many of them. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italy announces new security measures after Milan riots, deploying 500 soldiers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88c4788c7a397338597705bbd14c3731ceed65b48a88b184c326b340d7e9fc61</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:33:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-italy-announces-new-security-measures-after-milan-riots-deploying-500-soldiers--40cbfd38a691.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-italy-announces-new-security-measures-after-milan-riots-deploying-500-soldiers" /><summary type="html">Italy announced tougher security measures on Tuesday after weekend riots in Milan left more than 100 police officers injured and shops looted. The government will deploy 500 additional soldiers, impose harsher penalties for violent protesters and hold parents financially responsible for damage caused by minors.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Italy sends troops, toughens security laws after Milan clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e2e3bb0fc0cc6e27c011971c76c0b38bd9c84231ce132816d8c872284bde25e</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T20:09:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/italy-sends-troops-toughens-security-laws-after-milan-clashes--ad45dc4b7d94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/italy-sends-troops-toughens-security-laws-after-milan-clashes" /><summary type="html">Italy on Tuesday approved the deployment of 500 troops to Milan after violent clashes as fuel price protests hit pasta production and food deliveries in southern Italy. A cabinet meeting on Tuesday also approved a series of security measures, including making the detention of minors easier and introducing the crime of "violent participation in a demonstration". FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky meets Witkoff as US-Ukraine relations sink to new lows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44cf1200335850a77700ec9beb322a4f4f144aa0c425e0e3e4e74e08931b21e5</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T19:06:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelenskiy-meets-witkoff-as-us-ukraine-relations-sink-to-new-lows--95c89843b78c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelenskiy-meets-witkoff-as-us-ukraine-relations-sink-to-new-lows" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky was meeting US special envoy Steve Witkoff on Tuesday in a ​bid to rescue relations that have sunk to new lows as President Donald Trump has courted Moscow and Kyiv has complained about Washington withholding vital defences. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine ‘losing people and time’, Zelensky says after Oslo talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e293c72176fab82584fd9610f64e54e2f0341264e0ede857362a567c9c0ed22</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T14:11:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-oslo-for-talks-with-us-envoys-ukraine-claims-missile-holdup--27a933f0849a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-oslo-for-talks-with-us-envoys-ukraine-claims-missile-holdup" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has wrapped up talks with US envoys in Norway Tuesday where he was determined to put diplomacy back on a "more constructive path”, Oslo officials said.  Zelensky told a post-meeting press briefing that Ukraine was not losing the war but was “losing people and time”, adding that he was hopeful moving forward because “we have some clear ideas of how to get peace”.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Six years on, France remembers slain teacher Samuel Paty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1329b3895fd0e00192435dba87aedb59aac33befb67399ffce2c74a233602bf0</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T13:28:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261020-six-years-on-france-remembers-slain-teacher-samuel-paty--d4f09aa962ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261020-six-years-on-france-remembers-slain-teacher-samuel-paty" /><summary type="html">French schoolteacher Samuel Paty was killed on October 16, 2020 after false rumours circulated about racism following one of his lessons in which cartoons from the satirical publication Charlie Hebdo were shown. For the first time since his murder, journalists from France Télévisions were allowed to film inside the school where he taught in Conflans-Sainte-Honorine, near Paris. They met a new generation of young people, who are determined to play their part in the fight against terrorism.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>France imposes nightly curfews for 'as long as necessary' in Paris, other major cities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:975bd0fee3d9ba0b36e2f64d5c24854b2949582665f11f0c8a8ded8a7befca3d</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T02:51:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-live-curfews-come-into-effect-around-france-to-combat-looting--05cd1ff675ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-live-curfews-come-into-effect-around-france-to-combat-looting" /><summary type="html">French authorities announced fresh curfew orders across city centers of major cities including Paris, Lyon and Marseille for Tuesday night after Monday's curfew order calmed some of the country's most destructive rioting in recent years. Paris police said the curfew in two designated zones would remain in place "for as long as necessary". Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky accuses US of delaying missile deliveries as tensions rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3494f65b37a2aa89bda0d056983e990d3b4c461f5d60ac848c90cad8cf4ededf</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T01:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-accuses-us-of-delaying-missile-deliveries-as-tensions-rise--c2d39297890d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-accuses-us-of-delaying-missile-deliveries-as-tensions-rise" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky accused the US on Monday of holding up deliveries of Patriot interceptor missiles already paid for by European allies, as tensions with US President Donald Trump’s administration deepened over military aid and intelligence sharing.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU unveils strategy to bolster Arctic presence amid pressure from Russia and the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e383ed409e80f675d8cd08459b9d50734d7740e46541a5a910ac4bd6fb4f111e</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T01:35:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-eu-unveils-strategy-to-bolster-arctic-presence-amid-pressure-from-russia-and-the-us--42930b60ecd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-eu-unveils-strategy-to-bolster-arctic-presence-amid-pressure-from-russia-and-the-us" /><summary type="html">The European Union unveils its new "strategy for the Arctic" on Tuesday, aiming to step up its presence in the far north as melting ice opens new maritime routes, and tensions with Russia and the United States increasingly put the region in the geopolitical spotlight.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain floods kill four as torrential rain inundates eastern regions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4428bffd25c694a9bf77f7e94e2c95afbf509f11ad54d7c206c0251e780de02</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T21:39:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-spain-floods-kill-four-as-torrential-rain-inundates-eastern-regions--cc9d8cd8dd08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-spain-floods-kill-four-as-torrential-rain-inundates-eastern-regions" /><summary type="html">Torrential rain battered eastern Spain on Monday, killing at least four people in recent days as floodwaters swept away cars, submerged roads and stranded residents. Emergency crews carried out more than 400 rescues in Valencia, where rainfall reached 700 litres per square metre in 24 hours in some areas.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia-China-US summit would prolong the war, Kyiv says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21cf17d6c212f82c49bc8341bf9d3df9d9077b3d0c4a7ea24e0e94b54b838e9c</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-china-us-summit-would-prolong-the-war-kyiv-says--45dc255a1fdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-china-us-summit-would-prolong-the-war-kyiv-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ⁠Foreign Minister ​Andrii Sybiha said on ​Monday that a summit between Russia, China ​and the ‌US would ⁠encourage President Vladimir Putin ‌to prolong the war. The ​Wall Street Journal reported that Putin had proposed a ​summit next month ​with US ​President Donald Trump and Chinese President ​Xi Jinping to negotiate an end to the war on terms ⁠that would favour Moscow. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says Starshield speed limits slowing down frontline response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4c485d814425cd1cc0b3260afe2b167118f77c6ec3648b79315abc6f7242ea0</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-starshield-speed-limits-slowing-down-frontline-response--337310623a55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-starshield-speed-limits-slowing-down-frontline-response" /><summary type="html">Speed limits on a US military grade satellite system are hindering Ukrainian forces' ability to coordinate drone strikes against Russian forces, President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Monday. Zelensky said frontline units had reported that the Starshield equipment "stops functioning at speeds of 130-160 kilometres (80-100 miles) per hour in various sectors of the front". Separately, a Ukrainian army brigade has announced the rescue of a wounded soldier from the front line using an aerial drone, describing the evacuation as the first of its kind. The brigade published a video showing the drone lowering itself to the ground, before a man in combat gear fastens himself to a winch onboard and is lifted upwards. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine deploys drone to airlift wounded soldier in 'world-first' operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73cf1f474fbbcddd0847515c23b87c25e230acfb4e1f59d8de24e517a79895df</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:44:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-ukraine-deploys-drone-airlift-wounded-soldier-world-first-operation--49138a212dd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-ukraine-deploys-drone-airlift-wounded-soldier-world-first-operation" /><summary type="html">Ukraine has evacuated a wounded soldier from the front line using an aerial drone in what a Ukrainian army brigade has described as a world-first operation. The successful mission highlights the growing role of unmanned technology in battlefield evacuations as drones continue to shape the conflict between Ukraine and Russia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Quite horrifying': Afghan economic crisis leaves EU deportees with 'very little' to return to</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c5b0d656e77db99cb85c3cbf1a4f69f74d0faa13d70ceb38e8280bbc377af45</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T06:33:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-quite-horrifying-afghan-economic-crisis-leaves-eu-deportees-with-very-little-to-return-to-1--9ae856effb69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-quite-horrifying-afghan-economic-crisis-leaves-eu-deportees-with-very-little-to-return-to-1" /><summary type="html">Europe's increasingly pragmatic engagement with Afghanistan's Taliban rulers is exposing a fundamental contradiction between diplomatic non-recognition and political necessity. In an investigation for The New York Times, Pakistan and Afghanistan bureau chief Elian Peltier reveals how European governments are quietly expanding negotiations with the Taliban over migrant deportations, diplomatic representation and economic assistance. “Even though on paper European governments do not recognise the Taliban administration, in practice they meet much more frequently than most of us know,” Peltier explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Kyiv as Rubio urges Ukraine's Zelensky to 'focus' on ending war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:347f5b12e71f100a49238fee662f8cbbdc73e9db3a131ca49699381a2a9a349e</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T06:00:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-live-russian-strikes-pound-kyiv-as-rubio-denies-us-paused-intel-sharing-with-ukraine--f6c4065d175c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-live-russian-strikes-pound-kyiv-as-rubio-denies-us-paused-intel-sharing-with-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russia on Monday said it carried out a "massive strike" on targets in Kyiv and its region as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio denied that Washington had paused intelligence sharing with Ukraine and urged its President Volodymyr Zelensky to focus on ending the war.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky holds US talks as Trump accuses him of not wanting peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b003d24dbf3effdb4bd86387b9e64a18570ac52145a9a47a006f9b1488f37e5</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T21:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions--71a514130b55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky spoke with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner on Sunday amid tensions after US President Donald Trump accused Kyiv of resisting peace with Russia. The talks came as both sides exchanged attacks on energy infrastructure, while Washington's easing of Russian sanctions raised concerns among European allies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drone attack on Saint Petersburg kills one, sets refinery ablaze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01b6f1ab86c7c20939489efcb3cac888d604a47e0086fc88f166cd8e5127bb97</id><updated>2026-10-21T20:15:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T12:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack--5c56492efee9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack" /><summary type="html">A large-scale Ukrainian drone attack on Russia's second-largest city Saint Petersburg killed at least one person and hospitalised another five on Sunday. The attack – which also sparked fires at an oil refinery and depot – comes as Kyiv accused Russia of violating Washington's "energy ceasefire" dozens of times.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
